Factors which can be culled out as required to be kept in mind while awarding interim maintenance are as under:-
 (i) Status of the parties;
 (ii) Reasonable wants of the claimant;
 (iii) The income and property of the claimant;
 (iv) Number of persons to be maintained by the husband;
 (v) Liabilities, if any, of the husband;
 (vi) The amount required by the wife to live a similar life- style as she enjoyed in the matrimonial home keeping in view food, clothing, shelter,
educational and medical needs of the wife and the children, if any, residing with the wife."
Ram Pal Verma vs Of on 13 October, 2015 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/2121207/
